    "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
    "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued October 21 at 1:43PM AKDT until October 24 at 7:00AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
    "description": "* WHAT...Water levels most likely around 1.0 to 2.0 feet above\nthe normal highest tide line, with highest water levels\nexpected near Togiak.\n\n* WHERE...Northern Bristol Bay Coast.\n\n* WHEN...10 AM Friday to 7AM Saturday\n\n* IMPACTS...Nuisance flooding of low lying areas. Coastal\nerosion is possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A Bering front arrives to the Southwest\nAlaska coast Friday morning, bringing a prolonged period of\nstrong southerly winds towards the coast. These winds will\nresult in elevated water levels and high surf. This period of\nwinds will coincide with two tidal cycles and push water\nlevels 1.0 to 2.0 feet above the normal highest tide line.\nWater levels are expected to quickly drop off Saturday morning\nas winds decrease, alleviating coastal concerns.",
    "instruction": "Precautions should be taken to protect property.",
    "response": "Avoid",
